# Compiled binaries. `wails build` writes into build/bin; a bare `go build`
# in the repository root drops the executable next to main.go.
/build/bin/
/debark-gui
/debark-gui.exe

# The frontend bundle. Generated by `make frontend` (hack/copyfrontend) as a
# plain copy of frontend/index.html, frontend/src and frontend/wailsjs — it is
# output, never a source of truth, and editing it is always a mistake.
#
# .gitkeep is the exception and is committed deliberately: main.go embeds this
# directory with `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`, and go:embed fails the build
# on a directory that does not exist. Without a committed file here, a fresh
# clone would not compile until someone happened to run the frontend build.
#
# Written as `/*` plus a negation rather than `/frontend/dist/`: git does not
# descend into an ignored directory, so a trailing-slash rule makes the
# re-inclusion below unreachable.
/frontend/dist/*
!/frontend/dist/.gitkeep

# Generated by `wails build --nsis`. Wails rewrites this file from its own
# template on every NSIS build (nsis_installer.go calls
# ReadOriginalFileWithProjectDataAndSave on it, where project.nsi gets a plain
# ReadFile and is left alone), so a committed copy is output masquerading as
# source. The stock template it regenerates sets REQUEST_EXECUTION_LEVEL
# "admin" and runs Microsoft's online WebView2 installer; the decisions this
# project needs instead live in project.nsi, which is committed and is not
# regenerated. See docs/packaging.md.
/build/windows/installer/wails_tools.nsh

# Release output. goreleaser writes archives, checksums, signatures and the
# .deb into dist/, and `make snapshot` runs it locally — so this fills up on a
# developer machine, not only in CI. It is build output like build/bin above;
# the difference is that a stray untracked dist/ sits in `git status` looking
# like something to add, which is precisely the mistake this repository's
# commit discipline exists to prevent.
/dist/

# frontend/wailsjs/ is NOT ignored. Those are Wails' generated Go bindings for
# the frontend, and they are committed on purpose so that a fresh clone builds
# and runs without anyone first installing the wails CLI and running
# `wails generate module`. Regenerate and commit them when bindings change.

# Test and coverage output.
/coverage.out
*.test

# node_modules is NOT ignored, also on purpose. This project has zero npm
# dependencies and no JavaScript build step; if a node_modules/ ever appears
# in `git status`, that is a defect to investigate, not noise to hide.

# Editor and OS cruft.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Browser profiles left behind by headless test harnesses. The screen tracks
# drive a real browser to verify rendering, and Chrome writes a profile
# wherever it is pointed; none of it belongs in the repository.
cdp/
.chrome-profile/

# Python bytecode generated by the native review harness.
__pycache__/
